modifications:
- Removed dynamic `oxfmt` import in src/converter/index.ts (formatHtml is now a no-op).
- Dropped src/converter/shape-code.ts and src/converter/semantics-store.ts (unused by Penpot integration; they were the only other oxfmt consumers).
- Dropped all *.test.ts and *.integration.test.ts files (upstream test suite stays in penpot-tools).
- Wrote a self-contained tsconfig.json targeting ES2022 ESM with declarations.
- Extended `extractAllTokens` (src/converter/tokens.ts) to resolve every applied
  token attribute Penpot supports — opacity, shadow, composite typography,
  fontWeight and x/y — which were previously dropped, and added `opacity`/`shadow`
  to `TokenCategory`. Only `dist/converter/tokens.*` and `dist/penpot.types.d.ts`
  were re-emitted (the rest of `dist` is left as-is to avoid reverting unrelated
  src/dist drift in this snapshot).
